# Documentation Sync

When implementing or modifying features, keep documentation updated.

## Required Updates

When changing code in `lib/`:
- Update relevant sections in `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, or `QUICKSTART.md`
- Add new features to `CHEATSHEET.md` if applicable
- Document new environment variables in `.env.example`

## Checklist

Before completing any feature work:
- [ ] Public API changes documented
- [ ] New modules/bots have docstrings (`@moduledoc`, `@doc`)
- [ ] New config options added to `.env.example` with comments
- [ ] Architecture changes reflected in `ARCHITECTURE.md`

## Example

```elixir
# When adding a new bot, include module documentation:
defmodule BotArmy.Bots.NewBot do
  @moduledoc """
  Handles [describe purpose].

  ## Configuration
  - `NEW_BOT_INTERVAL` - How often to run (default: 5 minutes)

  ## Events
  - Subscribes to: `some.event`
  - Publishes: `new_bot.result`
  """
end
```

Then update `ARCHITECTURE.md` with the new bot's role in the system.
